# Normalise line endings in the repo, and check text files out with LF on
# every platform. Two things here are load-bearing rather than cosmetic:
#
#   - Generated files. `gen:law-vectors` and `sync-scenarios.mjs` both write
#     LF. Without this, git hands a Windows checkout CRLF, the generators
#     rewrite LF, and every regeneration reports a diff that is nothing but
#     line endings. That makes `sync-scenarios --check` in CI meaningless
#     (it can't tell a stale file from a checkout artefact) and buries any
#     real change in noise.
#
#   - Shell scripts. A CRLF shebang line makes a script unrunnable in CI.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ico           binary

# Generated — collapse in review diffs, but still tracked and still checked.
contracts/law/test/vectors/*.json  linguist-generated=true
apps/web/public/scenarios/*.json   linguist-generated=true
pnpm-lock.yaml                     linguist-generated=true
